{
  "configuration_id": "config_025",
  "reason": "Existing evidence shows the best current setup is multimodal multiprofile with PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, and weighted fusion (accuracy 0.639, F1 0.620), while RNA-only multiprofile avgpool reaches 0.591 and image-only ResNet50 is much weaker. The key uncertainty is whether the image representation is limiting the multimodal gain, since ResNet50 performs poorly as an image-only model. This experiment tests that directly by replacing ResNet50 with imagenet_vit_l while keeping the otherwise best-known settings fixed: PCA RNA encoder, multiprofile, avgpool aggregation, and weighted fusion. It is the best next experiment because it is a clean one-factor extension of the current best configuration, isolates the effect of image representation, and can either improve performance or clarify whether image features are the bottleneck without confounding changes to profile, aggregation, or fusion."
}

